issue=f'''<!-- L3S3 ISSUE START --><article class="card build-notice" id="brakeselection-sidebearers"><p class="eyebrow">3L.3-S3 · NEW PIECEWISE BODY / TRUCK SUPPORT LAW · 19 OCTOBER 2026</p><h2>The wheels can stay loaded while the center bearing unloads.</h2><p>Extends the previous linear roll-boundary study with explicit left/right sidebearer gaps and compression forces, center-bearing load sharing and the external body-roll reaction.13synthetic analytical fixtures exercise onset, left/right behavior, zero-gap comparison and center-contact loss.</p><p><strong>No support hardware or mount dimensions are selected.</strong> This is an ideal gapped frictionless comparison with an imposed body angle—not the actual coach/other-truck roll solution or a model of a preloaded constant-contact product. The real center bearing, retained pivot, sidebearers and actual coil stations remain open.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="assets/truck-support-l3s3/sidebearer_equilibrium.py">Editable piecewise engine</a><a class="button" href="assets/truck-support-l3s3/synthetic-support-fixtures.json">Exact synthetic inputs</a><a class="button" href="assets/truck-support-l3s3/support-results.json">Every contact / reaction / branch</a><a class="button" href="#brakeselection-twist">Preserved four-corner model</a></div></article><article class="card"><h2>How the support load is shared</h2><p>For relative rollr=φ_truck−φ_body: right compressionδ_R=b_R·r−g_R, leftδ_L=−b_L·r−g_L. Each sidebearer carriesk·max(δ,0), never tension. Its moment on the truck isM_side=b_R·F_R−b_L·F_L.</p><p>The prescribed body downforce enters the truck equilibrium <strong>once</strong>. Sidebearers redistribute that load: R_center=W_body−F_R−F_L. Do not add sidebearer vertical forces on top of the original body force or subtract sprung truck-frame weight from centerR.</p><p>For each assumed contact branch, Kφ=Σk·b² and its equivalent reference includes the active gap terms. The engine enumerates all4branches, checks gap/moment consistency and deduplicates the same zero-force boundary solution. At exact onset, multiple branch labels do not mean multiple physical equilibria.</p><p><strong>External reaction is explicit:</strong> the prescribed body needs an external roll moment−M_side to balance its upward side-contact couple. Other-truck/body torsion and the actual source of that reaction are not solved here. Positive force/moment balance is not free-body whole-coach stability.</p></article><article class="card" id="brakeselection-sidebearer-cases"><h2>Synthetic support checks—not proposed setup values</h2><p>RetainS2base springs/contact geometry and30kN body reaction plus10kN sprung truck weight and8kN unsprung total. Sidebearer halfspan0.5m, rate900,000N/m and gaps5mm are deliberate test constants, not project mount positions or setup instructions. The center-unload diagnostic reduces only body reaction to2kN.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Synthetic fixture</th><th>Truck roll slope</th><th>Right / left sidebearer kN</th><th>Center kN</th><th>Wheel vertical min / max kN</th><th>Contact regime only</th></tr></thead><tbody>{rows}</tbody></table></div><p>At railroll0.020/bodyroll0, the5mmgap example yields truckroll0.015, right side force2.25kN, center27.75kN and side moment1.125kNm. Reducing body reaction to2kN leaves positive wheel reactions but predicts center−0.25kN: <strong>the maintained-center-contact assumption fails.</strong> No lifted-center redistribution, retained-pivot tension capacity or safety permission is inferred.</p><p>Zero gap reproduces the prior linear-restraint result, but still has zero preload. It must not be substituted for a real constant-contact bearing’s preload, setup, friction or wear law. Pure diagonal warp remains unchanged when these symmetric positive gaps stay open; sidebearers cannot be presumed to cure track twist.</p></article><article class="card"><h2>Decisions required before drawing the mounts</h2><ul>{''.join('<li><strong>'+E(subject)+':</strong> '+E(text)+'</li>' for id,subject,text in decisions)}</ul><h3>Model limits</h3><ul>{''.join('<li>'+E(s)+'</li>' for s in limits)}</ul><p>Actual manufacturer context checked19October2026: <a href="https://www.wabteccorp.com/freight-car/truck-systems/constant-contact-side-bearings" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wabtec constant-contact family</a> and <a href="https://stucki.com/product-category/running-gear/side-bearings/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Stucki side-bearing family</a>. These establish real product categories only, not selection/compatibility/ratings for this36in train. A searched Stucki brochure link returned404; no cached setup/preload values were adopted.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="assets/truck-support-l3s3/method-sources-and-limitations.json">Derivation / sources / assumptions</a><a class="button" href="assets/truck-support-l3s3/support-interface-decisions.json">Exact support / station decisions</a><a class="button" href="assets/truck-support-l3s3/test_support.py">Independent analytical tests</a><a class="button" href="assets/truck-support-l3s3/build_issue.py">Editable issue source</a></div><p>3L.3-S3 completes this bounded support-law mechanics issue, not a complete truck or fabrication-ready suspension mounting set. No new physical geometry or actual test is claimed. Browser interaction remains unverified after managed preview failure. Next: controlled wheelset/axlebox/D1 and accepted whole-truck load/motion/support-interface closure; reassess genuinely independent work before making more models or drawings.</p></article><!-- L3S3 ISSUE END -->'''
